# e2 studio / RASC build output.
#
# Debug/ is where e2 emits the generated flash layout (bsp_linker_info.h,
# memory_regions.ld, fsp_gen.ld) alongside the object files. The TF-M port READS those
# text files, so a fresh clone needs the solution built in e2 once before cmake will
# configure - that is by design, and is why building here is a documented prerequisite
# rather than something the repo carries.
#
# Note the deliberate exception elsewhere: the bundled project set planned for
# platform/ext/target/renesas/ra6e1/ in the TF-M repo DOES keep those three text files,
# so it builds out of the box. That is a different repo; this rule stands here.
Debug/

# J-Link session logs, written into whichever project was launched.
# NOT *.jlink - those are flash/debug command SCRIPTS (the per-project Debug_SSD and
# ra*_TFM* ones) and are tracked deliberately.
JLinkLog.log

# Compiled output. Nothing built should be committed.
*.o
*.a
*.elf
*.axf
*.map
*.srec
*.hex
*.bin
*.sbd
*.rpd

# Python bytecode. imgtool is invoked from ra6e1_mcuboot/ra/mcu-tools during
# signing, which leaves __pycache__ inside the vendored MCUboot copy.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT PART OF THE DELIVERABLE
#
# Working material that is useful here and meaningless to anyone receiving the port.
# Everything below stays on disk and out of the repository.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Agent session state.
.claude/

# Trigger file: an empty document that asks for the next review round. It carries no
# content, and build_doc_html.py skips it by name for the same reason.
START_REVIEW.md

# Outside-reviewer snapshots: the doc-accuracy rounds and the 2026-10 technical and
# upstream-comparison reviews, with their CSVs and the triage generated from them.
# check_docs.py already exempts these paths from reference resolution (PATH_EXEMPT).
docs/artifacts/
docs/artifacts_v*/
docs/General_tech_review/

# Scratch e2 project for TrustZone experiments. Not referenced by the port.
tz_test/

# Plans and process notes. Maintainer material: a schedule, a documentation plan and the
# prose-style instruction the documents are edited against. They stay on disk and out of the
# deliverable, like the review snapshots above.
PROJECT_PLAN.md
PROJECT_PLAN.html
DOCUMENTATION_PLAN.md
docs/STYLE_EDIT_PROMPT.md

# Dormant-part and descoped design notes. RA6E1 is reference only and runs an older FSP pack;
# the dual-core work was descoped; the flash-map review's outcome is in DESIGN.md section 4 and
# its one residual check is in FSP_UPREV_CHECKLIST.md.
RA6E1_SOLUTION.md
RA8x2_DUAL_CORE_DESIGN.md
FLASH_MAP_OWNERSHIP.md

# The rendered mirror of every document. It is generated, it doubles the change surface, and a
# full mirror leaks the documents above. Run scripts/build_doc_html.py to produce it - the
# course under docs/learning/ links into it - and generate it at packaging time.
docs/learning/ref/
